<!--
    Connector: Database (generic — covers MySQL, PostgreSQL, MSSQL, Oracle, MariaDB)
    Registry key: database (or mysql / postgresql / mssql / oracle-db)
    Connector: mule-db-connector 1.14.0  (org.mule.connectors)
    Namespace: xmlns:db="http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/db"
    Schema:    http://www.mulesoft.org/schema/mule/db/current/mule-db.xsd
    TODO: Verify exact patch version at https://anypoint.mulesoft.com/exchange/org.mule.connectors/mule-db-connector/

    DRIVER NOTES by database:
      MySQL:      com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver   (add mysql-connector-j to pom.xml)
      PostgreSQL: org.postgresql.Driver       (add postgresql to pom.xml)
      MSSQL:      com.microsoft.sqlserver.jdbc.SQLServerDriver (add mssql-jdbc to pom.xml)
      Oracle:     oracle.jdbc.OracleDriver    ← CANNOT go in pom.xml (Oracle license)
                  Place ojdbc11.jar in shared lib folder on CloudHub 2.0
      MariaDB:    org.mariadb.jdbc.Driver     (add mariadb-java-client to pom.xml)

    Properties required in {env}.yaml:
      db.host      → database hostname
      db.port      → port (MySQL: 3306, PG: 5432, MSSQL: 1433, Oracle: 1521)
      db.name      → database/schema name
      db.user      → service account username (via Secrets Manager for prod)
      db.password  → via Secrets Manager (never in property files for prod)

    Connection pool: Default pool is 5 connections — tune for production load.
    Always use prepared statements (parameterized queries) — no string concatenation (SQL injection).
-->

